From decfb7f5fdd18ac7d0f77dce70748f51158b847e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:53:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: re-point boxes at the fragments of a reused layout
 result

A formatting context keeps two cached layout results, one from measuring
it and one from its final layout, so that nested flex containers don't
take time exponential in their depth. Laying the context out at another
size in between replaced the fragments its descendant boxes keep for
layout queries, so reusing the other result left them pointing at
fragments that are not in the fragment tree: getBoundingClientRect() on a
cell of a stretched table in a column flexbox returned an empty rectangle
at the origin.

Each fragment now refers back to the fragment list of the box it was made
for. Reusing a cached result makes the fragments in it the fragments of
their boxes again, unless the box already knows that its descendants hold
the fragments of that result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
